  "authored_scope": "Supported: 1..3 independent scenes per grid; all 4 line directions with both snake sides; 4-connected target blobs up to 4x4 whose snake-side outline changes by at most 1 per layer; hug offsets 0..5 from the anchor; delta=0 gaps of 2..4, otherwise fully diagonal approaches including gap 1 with the target touching the anchor; leave tails 0..5; clipping at the far edge along the line direction; ~80% border-anchored lines; optional distractor blobs farther than each anchor's target; random palettes; grids 7..30 per side, square or non-square. Synthetic extensions beyond the fixtures: sizes 28..30, non-square grids, floating lines, distractors, tails of 4..5. Deliberately not supported: hug columns on the line side of the anchor; sideways approaches with slack, where the early-vs-late choice is untaught; sideways clipping; scenes that touch one another; more than 3 scenes.",
  "authored_constraints": [
    "Scenes are separated by Chebyshev distance >= 2 including their output paths, so there is no cross-scene connectivity and no path overwrites another scene.",
    "The three colours of a scene are distinct and differ from the background; the background is the strict majority colour.",
    "The structural reading must find exactly the intended line/snake attachments. Each anchor must have a unique nearest non-line, non-snake object, and that object must be its own target.",
    "The snake lies within the line's span on the snake side, is not straight, and does not touch the line's far end perpendicularly.",
    "The path's sideways coordinate stays in bounds; clipping happens only along the line direction.",
    "The snake length always reaches at least one hug layer.",
    "Width, height, background and num_scenes must be real ints (bools and floats are rejected); explicit scenes are bounds- and palette-checked.",
    "All rejection loops are bounded (500 outer attempts, 60 placements per scene, 100 snake walks, 40 tries per distractor)."
  ],
